Exploration complete. Here is the full report on the household logic in this Spring PetClinic REST / OfficeFloor codebase.

## Build system & test command (item 8)
Maven (with wrapper). No Gradle files exist. `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`, `mvnw`, `mvnw.cmd`, `.mvn/`.
- Run everything: `./mvnw test`
- Run the household acceptance test only: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`
- The class holding the household test is `AcceptanceTest`; its shared harness is `AcceptanceBase` (uses `@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `@Transactional`, MockMvc against `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`).

## Owner-creation endpoint (item 6)
`POST /api/owners` is defined entirely in YAML at
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. It is a linear OfficeFloor pipeline, guarded by `authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"`. The wired steps in order:
`BuildOwner → EnsureOwnerPostcode → AdjustOwnerRegistrationDate → NormalizeOwnerTelephone → NormalizeOwnerAddress → EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity → EnsureCityHasCapacity → EnsureDailyRegistrationCapacity → AssignOwnerCustomerCode → AssignOwnerNamesakeCount → AssignOwnerHouseholdSize → SaveOwner → AuditOwnerCreated → RespondWithOwnerCreated`.

The function classes live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`.

## Key architectural finding — the household duplicate check and householdId assignment are NOT wired in
The pipeline uses `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity`, and `setHouseholdId(...)` is only ever called inside `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold`, which is **not referenced by any YAML** (grep of `officefloor/rest/` for these function names matched only `owners.POST.yml`, and that file wires `ensureUniqueIdentity`, not household/email/telephone). So `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold`, `EnsureUniqueOwnerEmail`, and `EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone` are orphaned relative to the live endpoint. Consequences in the running pipeline:
- `householdId` is never set → stays `null`.
- `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize` therefore always yields `1` (its `getHouseholdId() != null` guard is false).
- `IdentityKey`'s trailing `householdId` segment is always empty.
- The acceptance test `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` reads back `householdId` and would not get the deterministic value it asserts.

There is also a spec/impl mismatch: the test doc, `openapi.yml`, and `PossibleDuplicate` all describe household/duplicates keyed on **(lastName, postcode)**, but `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold` computes the household hash from **(lastName, address)**.

## 3. How householdId is generated/assigned
Only in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold.java` (not wired):
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateHouseholdException {
    String household = household(owner);
    owner.setHouseholdId(Integer.toHexString(household.hashCode()).toUpperCase());
    if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
        return;
    }
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (!Objects.equals(existing.getId(), owner.getId())
                && household.equals(household(existing))) {
            throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(
                    "Another owner already shares this last name and address");
        }
    }
}
private static String household(Owner owner) {
    return normalize(owner.getLastName()) + '\n' + normalize(owner.getAddress());
}
private static String normalize(String value) {
    return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
}
```
So householdId = uppercase hex of `String.hashCode()` over `normalize(lastName) + "\n" + normalize(address)`. Note it uses address, not postcode. The `household_id` column is on the `Owner` entity (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`, field `householdId`, getter/setter lines 66-67, 142-148); `lastName` is on `Person` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`).

## 4. How duplicate detection works
Two mechanisms:

Hard duplicates (wired) — `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity` + `IdentityKey`:
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java`
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateIdentityException {
    String identityKey = IdentityKey.of(owner);
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (!Objects.equals(existing.getId(), owner.getId())
                && identityKey.equals(IdentityKey.of(existing))) {
            throw new DuplicateIdentityException("An owner with the same identity already exists");
        }
    }
}
```
